# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Caddy reverse proxy — one front door, automatic HTTPS for every app.
#
# Caddy fetches and renews a free Let's Encrypt certificate for every domain
# listed below, on its own, with zero config beyond the domain name. That single
# feature is why this is the lean choice: no certbot, no cron, no renewal
# scripts, no nginx TLS block to hand-edit ten times.
#
# HOW ROUTING WORKS: a request arrives for one of these domains; Caddy terminates
# TLS and forwards the plain HTTP to the matching app container by its service
# name and internal port (every app listens on 3000 INSIDE its own container —
# they do not collide because each is in its own network namespace).
#
# TO ADD AN APP: copy a block, change the domain and the `reverse_proxy` target
# to the new service name, add the matching service in docker-compose.multi.yml,
# and `docker compose up -d`. Caddy issues the certificate on first request.
#
# ⚠️ DNS FIRST: each domain's A record must already point at this server's IP,
# or Let's Encrypt cannot validate it and the certificate request fails.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Global options
{
	# The address Let's Encrypt emails about expiring certs / rate limits.
	email admin@mountolympusdetailing.com
	# Uncomment while testing to avoid Let's Encrypt's rate limits (5 certs per
	# domain per week). Issues untrusted staging certs — re-comment for real ones.
	# acme_ca https://acme-staging-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory
}

# ── App 1 — Mount Olympus Detailing ──────────────────────────────────────────
mountolympusdetailing.com, www.mountolympusdetailing.com {
	reverse_proxy app-mountolympus:3000
	encode zstd gzip
	# Uploaded photos and the app's own assets can be cached hard; HTML cannot
	# (it is server-rendered per request). Next.js already sends correct
	# Cache-Control headers, so we simply pass them through.
}

# ── App 2 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# client-two.com, www.client-two.com {
# 	reverse_proxy app-client-two:3000
# 	encode zstd gzip
# }

# ── App 3 … App 10 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Duplicate the block above per app, or let scripts/new-tenant.sh do it. Ten
# domains here = ten apps, each with its own auto-renewing certificate, behind
# this one proxy.

# ── NEW-TENANT-SITE (do not remove this line) ────────────────────────────────
# scripts/new-tenant.sh inserts each new app's site block ABOVE this marker.
